NAME
       selinuxenabled - tell scripts whether SELinux is enabled

SYNOPSIS
       selinuxenabled

DESCRIPTION
       selinuxenabled prints nothing. Its exit status is 0 when SELinux is
       enabled (enforcing or permissive) and 1 when it is disabled, which
       suits if-tests in scripts.

EXAMPLES
           if selinuxenabled; then restorecon -R /srv/web; fi

SEE ALSO
       getenforce(8), sestatus(8)
